  "result": "The fix is in place: the typecheck and lint are clean, and the suite has 614 passing and 3 failing. The 3 failures are existing tests that assert behaviour the spec forbids, so I left them as they are.\n\nThose three tests need updating by whoever owns them:\n- `tests/lib/permissions.ownership.test.ts`, \"lets a recipient manage their own notification\", asserts a viewer can manage another member's notification.\n- `tests/services/notification-service.test.ts`, \"creates one notification per mentioned user\" and \"always records the in-app notification\", list another member's inbox as the owner.\n\nI also ran a temporary test covering each reported item, and all of it passed. I deleted it afterwards.\n\nTwo choices you may want to redirect:\n- Plan-limit alerts are keyed by resource (projects, seats, issues per project, storage, webhooks), not by project. Issues in two different projects share one open alert.\n- Alerts already stored with the old `/issues/…` hrefs are not rewritten. Only new rows get the correct links.",
